Teach TQt3's OS-detection macro about substrate.

ntqglobal.h #errors out ("not been ported to this OS") unless it can map
the build's predefined compiler macros onto a Q_OS_* identity.  substrate
is a POSIX/ELF, Linux-like target, so map __substrate__ (defined by the
substrate-g++ mkspec via -D__substrate__) onto Q_OS_LINUX.

Patch only src/tools/ntqglobal.h: include/ntqglobal.h is a symlink to it
(patch(1) refuses to patch symlinks), and configure regenerates the
include/ copy from src/tools during the build.

--- a/src/tools/ntqglobal.h
+++ b/src/tools/ntqglobal.h
@@ -135,6 +135,8 @@
 #elif defined(__svr4__) && defined(i386) /* Open UNIX 8 + GCC */
 #  define Q_OS_UNIXWARE
 #  define Q_OS_UNIXWARE7
+#elif defined(__substrate__)
+#  define Q_OS_LINUX		/* substrate: POSIX/ELF, Linux-like */
 #elif defined(__MAKEDEPEND__)
 #else
 #  error "TQt has not been ported to this OS - talk to qt-bugs@trolltech.com"
